      "problem": "$\\int (5{csch}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)=-{csch}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{csch}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5(-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)-(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
